# Components are pure Roc functions

`@component` lowers to a function that returns `Html`. Given the same props and
body, it produces the same markup. That is why fixtures, `rocci view`, and HTTP
handlers can share one renderer.

Effects belong in `@init` and handlers: SQLite, `Stderr.line!`, reading
`request`. A component that logged or wrote the database would make preview,
tests, and live streams lie about their inputs.

There is no runtime component registry and no implicit instance state. Compose
by calling functions, including qualified imports.

**Related:** [Why Roc](/docs/concepts/why-roc/),
[State and effects](/docs/concepts/state-and-effects/).
